\subsection{Prescriptive Results}\label{sec:prescriptive}

\paragraph{Entity-level construction (exploratory).}
We aggregate entities across samples, retaining those exceeding $\theta{=}2/N$, with LP-weighted or uniform scoring ($\theta$ stable in $[0.15, 0.35]$; Appendix~\ref{app:theta_sweep}).
LP-weighted construction yields $+1.40{\pm}0.51$\,pp on Few-NERD ($p{<}0.001$; Holm $p_{\text{adj}}{=}0.006$, $k{=}10$; Table~\ref{tab:entity_construction}), a smaller non-significant $+0.32$\,pp on SciERC, and no gain on CoNLL ($-0.39$\,pp).\footnote{Holm--Bonferroni \cite{holm1979simple} within families ($k{=}10$, $21$, $9$); global $k{=}57$: $p_{\text{adj}}{=}0.055$. Under BH FDR, $6/10$ construction comparisons reach FDR${<}0.05$ (Appendix~\ref{app:holm}).}
Under global Holm--Bonferroni ($k{=}57$), $p_{\text{adj}}{=}0.055$; we retain per-family correction ($k{=}10$) as quality estimation, selection, and construction test independent mechanisms.
These families operate at different mathematical granularity---population-level $\rho$ (QE), instance-level ranking (selection), and entity-level aggregation (construction)---addressing independent research questions. We acknowledge this partition was not pre-registered; the global $k{=}57$ figure provides a conservative bound.
Gains require both low degeneracy \textit{and} LP-F1 alignment (Few-NERD: $D{=}13$\%, headroom${=}12.4$\,pp);\footnote{Degenerate instances contribute $\Delta{=}0$ by construction; gains concentrate in the non-degenerate subset ($+3.36$\,pp SciERC, $+5.18$\,pp CoNLL, $+7.08$\,pp Few-NERD).} $k$ values are validated per family ($k{=}10$, $21$, $9$).
Construction and LP selection are complementary ($\rho_{\text{adj}}$: Few-NERD $0.516$, SciERC $0.167$); QE signals support selective prediction ($+5$--$8$\,pp F1 at 80\% coverage; Table~\ref{tab:cross_selection}).

\paragraph{Epoch confound on Few-NERD.}
Few-NERD uses 3 training epochs (vs.\ 5), yielding lower degeneracy ($13$\% vs.\ $31$\% at 5-epoch) and stronger LP selection ($+1.39$ vs.\ $+0.12{\pm}0.04$\,pp; Appendix~\ref{app:epoch_confound}). This sensitivity reinforces the diagnostic framework: favorable conditions (low degeneracy $+$ LP-F1 alignment) are fragile and training-sensitive, underscoring the framework's value for practitioners. The core negative finding (selection ${\leq}$ greedy under high degeneracy) is unaffected.

